.TH ZERO 4 "January 2026" "Substrate Kernel" "Device Drivers Manual"
.SH NAME
zero \- zero byte source
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /dev/zero
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B zero
device provides an endless supply of null bytes (0x00) when read.
Writes to
.B /dev/zero
are accepted and discarded (similar to
.BR /dev/null ).
.PP
This device is commonly used to:
.IP \(bu 2
Initialize memory regions with zeros via
.BR mmap (2)
.IP \(bu 2
Create sparse files or zero-filled files
.IP \(bu 2
Benchmark read performance
.PP
.SH EXAMPLE
Create a 1MB zero-filled file:
.PP
.nf
    dd if=/dev/zero of=zeros.bin bs=1M count=1
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /dev/zero
The zero device special file (character device, major 1, minor 5).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR null (4),
.BR mmap (2),
.BR intro (4)
